# scoped-session.tflw — CHECK-ONLY FIXTURE (`M154g` step 4a, `C94`): see `named-service.tflw` for
# what this directory is and why its configs are generated.
#
# `session scoped` is declared `for env one`. Under `--env two` the identical `as scoped` clause is
# a `TF028`, and the sibling `unscoped-session.tflw` — same clause shape, a session with no `for
# env` — stays clean under both. The pair is what separates the **scoping clause** from env
# selection itself: without it, a `TF028` under `--env two` is equally consistent with sessions
# simply not resolving in that env at all.

test "a scoped session resolves only in the envs its clause names" as scoped
  api GET /health
  expect status equals 200
